.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_SUPERLATTICE "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_superlattice (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_superlattice \- compute eigenstates of a Kronig-Penney superlattice.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_superlattice
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find the eigenstates of an infinite Kronig\-Penney superlattice.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.TP
\fB\-k\fR [ \fB\-\-wavevector\fR ] arg (=0)
Wave\-vector expressed relative to pi/L,
where L is period length
.TP
\fB\-a\fR [ \fB\-\-wellwidth\fR ] arg (=100)
Width of quantum well [angstrom].
.TP
\fB\-b\fR [ \fB\-\-barrierwidth\fR ] arg (=100)
Width of barrier [angstrom].
.TP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-wellmass\fR ] arg (=0.067)
Effective mass in well (relative to that of
a free electron)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR [ \fB\-\-barriermass\fR ] arg (=0.067) Effective mass in barrier (relative to that
of a free electron)
.TP
\fB\-\-outputpotential\fR
Output the potential profile for the system
to v.r
.TP
\fB\-p\fR [ \fB\-\-particle\fR ] arg (=e)
ID of particle to be used: 'e', 'h' or 'l',
for electrons, heavy holes or light holes
respectively.
.TP
\fB\-N\fR [ \fB\-\-nz\fR ] arg (=1000)
Number of spatial points for output file.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR [ \fB\-\-nst\fR ] arg (=1)
Number of states to find
.TP
\fB\-\-barrierpotential\fR arg (=100)
Barrier potential [meV]
.TP
\fB\-\-Ecutoff\fR arg
Cut\-off energy for solutions [meV]
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files:
   'E*.r' Energy of each state:
          Column 1: state index.
          Column 2: energy [meV].

The '*' is replaced by the particle ID.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute the first three states at Gamma (k = 0) using 150-angstrom wells and barriers with 100 meV confining potential:
   qwwad_ef_superlattice --wellwidth 150 --barrierwidth 150 --barrierpotential 100 --nst 3 --wavevector 0

Compute the ground state at X (k = pi/L) using 100-angstrom wells, 200-angstrom barriers and 100 meV confining potential:
   qwwad_ef_superlattice --wellwidth 100 --barrierwidth 200 --barrierpotential 100 --wavevector 1
